        "section": "robotics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Robotics - Kinematics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Kinematics answers one question: given joint angles, where is the end-effector?\nAnd its inverse: given a desired end-effector pose, what joint angles achieve it?"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-KINEMATICS.md#003",
      "path": [
        "01-KINEMATICS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:robotics:01-kinematics, git-history:robotics:01-kinematics]",
        "canonical_path": "robotics/01-KINEMATICS.md",
        "concepts": "[kinematics]",
        "current_path": "robotics/01-KINEMATICS.md",
        "id": "maxim:robotics:kinematics",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "robotics",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[kinematics]",
        "section": "robotics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Robotics - Kinematics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n+=========================================================================+\n|                         KINEMATICS LANDSCAPE                            |\n+=========================================================================+\n|                                                                         |\n|  FORWARD KINEMATICS (FK)                INVERSE KINEMATICS (IK)         |\n|  ========================               ========================         |\n|                                                                         |\n|  Input:  q = [q1, q2, ..., qn]          Input:  T (4x4 pose matrix)    |\n|          joint angles                            desired EE pose         |\n|          (n = DOF of robot)                                             |\n|                                                                         |\n|  Output: T_0n (4x4 matrix)              Output: q = [q1, q2, ..., qn]  |\n|          end-effector pose                       joint angles            |\n|          (position + orientation)                                        |\n|                                                                         |\n|  Always has a UNIQUE solution.          May have MULTIPLE solutions,    |\n|  O(n) computation.                      NO solution, or infinite        |\n|  Solved by DH transform chain.          solutions (redundant arms).     |\n|                                                                         |\n|  +----------+    DH chain     +----------+                              |\n|  | q1..qn   | ------------->  | T_0n     |    DIFFERENTIAL KINEMATICS   |\n|  | angles   |                 | 4x4 pose |    J(q): maps q_dot -> v_EE  |\n|  +----------+                 +----------+    Jacobian matrix           |\n|                                                                         |\n|  WORKSPACE ANALYSIS              SINGULARITIES                          |\n|  Reachable workspace:            J loses rank -> velocity               |\n|    set of all poses FK can       amplification -> infinite joint        |\n|    produce within joint limits   velocities for finite EE velocity      |\n|                                                                         |\n+=========================================================================+\n```"
    },
