        "section": "robotics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Robotics - Kinematics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "A rigid body pose in 3D is position (3 values) + orientation (3 values = 6 DOF for pose,\nbut orientation requires a 3x3 rotation matrix or quaternion to encode non-linearly)."
    },
    {
      "id": "01-KINEMATICS.md#008",
      "path": [
        "01-KINEMATICS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
