        "root_concepts": "[kinematics]",
        "section": "robotics",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Robotics - Kinematics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Rotation matrix encodes direction cosines. Three common parametrizations:\n- **Euler angles** (ZYX, ZYZ): 3 numbers, gimbal lock at singularity. Used in aerospace.\n- **Axis-angle**: axis n (unit vector) + angle theta. Compact. Used in optimization.\n- **Quaternion**: 4 numbers (w, x, y, z), |q|=1. No gimbal lock. Used in robotics control."
    }
